:: Define Activities [system] {"position":"625,0","size":"100,100"}
/* Activities ==================================================================
   What mom and sister can be doing, per character and keyed by id. The definitions are constants
   (setup); the game state only ever stores the id:
     - routines and plans       { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] }   (Define Schedule)
     - tasks and task stages    activity: "giving_massage0"                         (Define Tasks)
     - $mom.activity / $sister.activity, set from setup.npcNow by PassageReady

   setup.activities.<sysName>.<id> = {
       id:          "testing_prototype",     the same as the key. A trailing number is the stage of a task
       base:        "testing_prototype",      optional, shared by all stages of one activity, so interaction
                                              rules (blocked/only) can name every stage at once
       text:        "testing the prototype",  what the player reads ("Mom is here testing the prototype."),
                                              may contain variables
       locations:   [ setup.getLocationBySysName("kitchen") ],
                                              where she can be doing it (read by getActivitiesForLocation)
       when:        [ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 ],        optional: time slots in which a routine row that names only a
                                              place may pick it at random. Without it, it is never picked at
                                              random (task activities, sleeping, cooking, ...)
       duration:    [ 2, 3 ],                 optional: once a plan picks it, it lasts that many actions (random
                                              between the two) as long as the next rows allow it. Default 1
       media:      [ "testing_prototype0_0.jpg", "testing_prototype0_1.mp4" ],
                                              images/characters/<sysName>/activities/<file>
       cctv:        [ "testing_prototype0_0.mp4" ],
                                              images/characters/<sysName>/tasks/<file>. Empty: the camera
                                              shows the activity media instead
       cctvPassage: "Passage",                optional: where the CCTV arrow leads when no task stage names one

       Optional, per corruption stage of mom/sister ("Corruption stages" in Define NPCs). The key is the
       stage from which on it is used; the highest key up to her stage wins, below the lowest key the plain
       field above is used. Leave them out until a stage really looks different.
       stageText:   { 1: "watching TV in nothing but a long shirt" }
       stageMedia:  { 1: [ "watching_tv_s1_0.jpg" ] }        same folder as media
       stageCctv:   { 1: [ "watching_tv_s1_0.mp4" ] }        same folder as cctv
   }

   File names are <id>_<n>.<ext>, stage files <id>_s<stage>_<n>.<ext>. Any image or video format works
   (jpg, png, webp, gif, mp4, webm).
   An activity without files just shows no picture. Check the lists against the files on disk with
       node tools/activity-media.mjs

   Helpers:
   setup.getActivity(who, id)               the definition, or undefined (who = "mom", "sister" or the NPC)
   setup.getNpcActivity(npc)                the definition of what she is doing right now
   setup.activityText(who, id)              its display text (stageText of her stage if there is one),
                                            variables filled in
   setup.activityByStage(who, byStage)      the entry of a stageText/stageMedia/stageCctv object for her
                                            current corruption stage, or undefined
   setup.activityIs(who, id, list)          is the activity one of list (ids or bases)?
   setup.getActivitiesForLocation(who, location)
                                            every activity definition whose locations include that place
                                            (location object or id, compared with setup.sameLocation)
   setup.activityMedia(who, id [, kind [, random]])
                                            the path of one of its files: kind "media" (default) or "cctv"
                                            (falls back to media), the stage lists first if her corruption
                                            stage has one. The same file for the whole action, so
                                            panels that redraw do not flicker; a random one if random is
                                            true. "" when there is nothing to show
*/
